A||N||13||AgaricX||The adventure begins...||||1||
Z||000000||AgaricX||08-28-2001||04:08 PM||||Well.  How to start.<P>I have been reding Cliff's forum for... quite a long time.  I've been reading lots of articles, reviews, manuals, etc on our obsession - the Fiero for years.  I finally broke down and bought a fixer upper.  I'm elated, my significant other is in a constant state of rolling her eyes :-)<P>Anyway, I need you guys' opinion.  I got an '85SE.  It used to be auto, the previous owner swapped it for a 5spd Isuzu.  He jerked the 4cyl (still have it if anyone wants it) and put in a 3800 sII out of an '85 Camaro.  He had 2 cars, this one and a parts car.  I got both for $600.  The car runs great.  I have to push the clustch ALL THE WAY DOWN though.  HE did some interesting custom exhaust work (no muffler or CAT.  That makes it illegal here (TX) but not in Louisiana.  The paint is mostly oxidized, but thats ok... I would have had it repainted anyway.  Headliner's gone.  Seats need recovering.  No rust.<P>Now the question.  Was it a decent deal?  I have all the body panels (fair condition) off the 2nd fiero (Formula) as well as about 3/4 of the engine/tranny parts.  I have the dash and wiring harness and quite a bit more that I still need to inventory.<P>Also, where should I start as far as testing the car's integrity?  It sounds fine, if not loud.  No knocks.  The brakes are solid.  The 3800 had 35k on it when the swap was done a year ago.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ntfc.org/classifieds.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ntfc.org/classifieds.html</A>  for the ad I bought it from.  (its the one in Shreveport, LA)<P>Love the forum!  You guys have converted an import (Toyota Supra) fan to a devoted Fiero fanatic.  I'll have more questions, buit this'll do me for now.  Thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||08-28-2001||04:18 PM||||I think you did fine.  A useable car plus parts car for $600 is probably better than average.  Just be prepared to put lots of time into your car...  probably why your significant other is rolling her eyes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> right now.  ||||reg||14
Z||000002||BlackDragon||08-28-2001||08:12 PM||||i need the four cyl. does it run? what do you want for it? any idea what shipping would cost? im in murray ky 42071. if you could find out, i would appreciate it. email me to let me know something.<P>------------------<BR>You pull up to a stop light..........you hear an engine rev....you look over and see a hard core, riced out, shogun, eurostriped, 3 level spoiler, civic.....you think to yourself "this should be fun"......you rev your engine.....the light turns green, you pop the clutch......shift to 2nd........ 3rd....... 4th.... you are winning, then you smell it and realize something bad has happened..... you look over at your best friend in the passenger seat, he looks back and you say "damnit dude, why did you have to fart" :damon:||||reg||1
Z||000003||AgaricX||08-28-2001||09:58 PM||||It worked fine when it was taken out.  I also have the auto tranny. Both 85SE ~75k<P>I have NO clue about shipping.  Anyone else know?  I'm near Houston, TX.  Where could I check?||||reg||6
Z||000004||artherd||08-28-2001||10:26 PM||||Woah!  <P>You got a great deal on that engine alone, and got the rest of the car for FREE!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Welcome to the fourm, first thing is: replace your aluminum clutch pedal with a *steel* one, that will probally fix it!!<P>Second, let me drive it !  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Exhaust wise, you could always fab your own, or just take it to a (competent!!) muffler shop and say "make it legal and good" probally cost $5-800 or so.<P>Good luck, sounds like the rest of the work is going to be restoration/interior/paint.<P>When you're done you will have quite the car!<P>Best!!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AgaricX:<BR><B>Well.  How to start.<P>I have been reding Cliff's forum for... quite a long time.  I've been reading lots of articles, reviews, manuals, etc on our obsession - the Fiero for years.  I finally broke down and bought a fixer upper.  I'm elated, my significant other is in a constant state of rolling her eyes :-)<P>Anyway, I need you guys' opinion.  I got an '85SE.  It used to be auto, the previous owner swapped it for a 5spd Isuzu.  He jerked the 4cyl (still have it if anyone wants it) and put in a 3800 sII out of an '85 Camaro.  He had 2 cars, this one and a parts car.  I got both for $600.  The car runs great.  I have to push the clustch ALL THE WAY DOWN though.  HE did some interesting custom exhaust work (no muffler or CAT.  That makes it illegal here (TX) but not in Louisiana.  The paint is mostly oxidized, but thats ok... I would have had it repainted anyway.  Headliner's gone.  Seats need recovering.  No rust.<P>Now the question.  Was it a decent deal?  I have all the body panels (fair condition) off the 2nd fiero (Formula) as well as about 3/4 of the engine/tranny parts.  I have the dash and wiring harness and quite a bit more that I still need to inventory.<P>Also, where should I start as far as testing the car's integrity?  It sounds fine, if not loud.  No knocks.  The brakes are solid.  The 3800 had 35k on it when the swap was done a year ago.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ntfc.org/classifieds.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ntfc.org/classifieds.html</A>  for the ad I bought it from.  (its the one in Shreveport, LA)<P>Love the forum!  You guys have converted an import (Toyota Supra) fan to a devoted Fiero fanatic.  I'll have more questions, buit this'll do me for now.  Thanks!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000005||MrPBody||08-28-2001||10:43 PM||||Sounds like a good deal to me.  I paid more than twice that for my '85 SE . . . <I>without</I> a 3800!  But hey -- I sorta like my Duke.  Sorta.<P>Dang!  If you were closer to Georgia, I would make you a deal on that Formula chassis.<P>Welcome to the forum!<BR>||||reg||1
